    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "The policy commits over \u00a33.6 billion in new spending over three years, but the evidence provided does not show whether this is funded from existing budgets or borrowed. If prevention delivers savings on the current \u00a32.3 billion annual temporary-accommodation bill, the long-run debt path could improve \u2014 but the net fiscal position is unresolvable from the available evidence.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the \u00a33.6 billion spending commitment is funded (and from where) or adds to borrowing, and whether projected prevention savings materialise at a scale that offsets the upfront cost.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "tier": "stated",
        "claim": "The policy commits to ensuring sufficient financial resources for local authorities to end rough sleeping.",
        "evidence_id": "M",
        "quote": "ensuring sufficient financial resources for local authorities"
      },
